traceability.evidence:
Key implementation files and tests:

1) Rule implementation: src/rules/prefer-implements-annotation.ts
- New ESLint rule `prefer-implements-annotation` exists and is traced to this story:
  /**
   * @story docs/stories/010.3-DEV-MIGRATE-TO-IMPLEMENTS.story.md
   * @req REQ-OPTIONAL-WARNING
   * @req REQ-MULTI-STORY-DETECT
   * @req REQ-SINGLE-STORY-FIX
   * @req REQ-PRESERVE-FORMAT
   * @req REQ-VALID-OUTPUT
   * @req REQ-BACKWARD-COMP-VALIDATION
   * @req REQ-AUTO-FIX
   */
- Detection of legacy @story + @req and optional warning:
  - analyzeComment/processComment:
    ```ts
    const { hasStory, hasReq, hasImplements, storyPaths } = analyzeComment(comment);
    if (!hasStory || !hasReq) { return; }
    if (hasImplements) {
      context.report({ messageId: "cannotAutoFix", data: { reason: "comment mixes @story/@req with existing @implements annotations" } });
      return;
    }
    if (hasMultipleStories(storyPaths)) {
      context.report({ messageId: "multiStoryDetected" });
      return;
    }
    const fix = buildImplementsAutoFix(context, comment, storyPaths);
    context.report({ messageId: "preferImplements", fix: fix ?? undefined });
    ```
- Auto-fix implementation (REQ-AUTO-FIX, REQ-SINGLE-STORY-FIX, REQ-PRESERVE-FORMAT, REQ-VALID-OUTPUT):
  - collectStoryAndReqMetadata enforces simple forms:
    ```ts
    if (/^@story\b/.test(normalized)) {
      const parts = normalized.split(/\s+/);
      if (parts.length === MIN_STORY_TOKENS) { storyLineIndices.push(index); storyPath = parts[1]; } else { storyPath = null; }
    }
    if (/^@req\b/.test(normalized)) {
      const parts = normalized.split(/\s+/);
      if (parts.length === MIN_REQ_TOKENS) { reqLineIndices.push(index); reqIds.push(parts[1]); } else { storyPath = null; }
    }
    ```
  - buildImplementsAutoFix restricts to single-story, at least one @req, and simple tokens:
    ```ts
    if (storyPaths.size !== 1) return null;
    const { storyLineIndices, reqLineIndices, reqIds, storyPath } = collectStoryAndReqMetadata(comment);
    if (storyPaths.size !== 1 || storyLineIndices.length !== 1 || reqLineIndices.length < 1 || storyPath === null) {
      return null;
    }
    ```
  - applyImplementsReplacement preserves formatting and relative position:
    ```ts
    const implAnnotation = `@implements ${storyPath} ${reqIds.join(" ")}`;
    const storyRawLine = rawLines[storyIdx];
    const prefixMatch = storyRawLine.match(/^(\s*\*?\s*)/);
    const linePrefix = prefixMatch ? prefixMatch[1] : "";
    const implementsLine = `${linePrefix}${implAnnotation}`;
    rawLines.forEach((line, index) => {
      if (index === storyIdx) { fixedLines.push(implementsLine); return; }
      if (allIndicesToRemove.has(index)) { return; }
      fixedLines.push(line);
    });
    ```
- Multi-story detection and mixed patterns (REQ-MULTI-STORY-DETECT):
  ```ts
  const MULTI_STORY_THRESHOLD = 1;
  function hasMultipleStories(storyPaths: Set): boolean { return storyPaths.size > MULTI_STORY_THRESHOLD; }
  if (hasImplements) {
    context.report({ messageId: "cannotAutoFix", data: { reason: "comment mixes @story/@req with existing @implements annotations" } });
    return;
  }
  if (hasMultipleStories(storyPaths)) {
    context.report({ messageId: "multiStoryDetected" });
    return;
  }
  ```
- Rule metadata and messages:
  ```ts
  meta: {
    type: "suggestion",
    docs: { description: "Recommend using @implements...", recommended: false },
    fixable: "code",
    messages: {
      preferImplements: "Consider using @implements instead of @story + @req...",
      cannotAutoFix: "Cannot auto-fix: {{reason}}. Manual migration to @implements required.",
      multiStoryDetected: "Multiple @story annotations detected in the same comment block. Manually convert to separate @implements lines.",
    },
    schema: [],
  }
  ```
- Backward-compat behavior for non-eligible comments:
  - processComment returns early when either @story or @req is missing:
    `if (!hasStory || !hasReq) { return; }` → comments with only @story, only @req, or only @implements are untouched by this rule.

2) Rule exposure and default severity: src/index.ts
- Rule is included in RULE_NAMES and exported:
  ```ts
  const RULE_NAMES = [
    "require-story-annotation",
    ...,
    "prefer-implements-annotation",
  ] as const;
  ```
- Default severities used in plugin configs:
  ```ts
  const TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES: Readonly<Record> = {
    "traceability/require-story-annotation": "error",
    ...,
    "traceability/prefer-implements-annotation": "warn",
  } as const;
  const configs = {
    recommended: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()],
    strict: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()],
  };
  ```
- This means that when consumers use `traceability.configs.recommended` or `.strict`, `traceability/prefer-implements-annotation` is enabled at level "warn" by default.

3) Tests: tests/rules/prefer-implements-annotation.test.ts
- File is explicitly tied to the story:
  ```ts
  /**
   * Tests for: docs/stories/010.3-DEV-MIGRATE-TO-IMPLEMENTS.story.md
   * @story docs/stories/010.3-DEV-MIGRATE-TO-IMPLEMENTS.story.md
   * @req REQ-OPTIONAL-WARNING
   * @req REQ-MULTI-STORY-DETECT
   * @req REQ-CONFIG-SEVERITY
   */
  ```
- Valid cases confirming backward compatibility:
  - Only @story → no error.
  - Only @req → no error.
  - Only @implements → no error.
- Invalid cases verify:
  - Warning + auto-fix for single-story @story + @req:
    ```ts
    {
      name: "[REQ-OPTIONAL-WARNING] single-story @story + @req block triggers preferImplements message",
      code: `/**\n * @story ...\n * @req REQ-ANNOTATION-REQUIRED\n */\nfunction legacy() {}`,
      output: `/**\n * @implements ... REQ-ANNOTATION-REQUIRED\n */\nfunction legacy() {}`,
      errors: [{ messageId: "preferImplements" }],
    }
    ```
  - Auto-fix combining multiple @req into single @implements (REQ-SINGLE-STORY-FIX):
    ```ts
    {
      name: "single @story with multiple @req lines auto-fixes to single @implements line containing all REQ IDs",
      code: `/**\n * @story ...\n * @req REQ-ONE\n * @req REQ-TWO\n * @req REQ-THREE\n */\nfunction autoFixMultiReq() {}`,
      output: `/**\n * @implements ... REQ-ONE REQ-TWO REQ-THREE\n */\nfunction autoFixMultiReq() {}`,
      errors: [{ messageId: "preferImplements" }],
    }
    ```
  - Multi-story detection and mixed @implements:
    - Mixed @story/@req + @implements → `messageId: "cannotAutoFix"` with specific reason.
    - Multiple @story paths → `messageId: "multiStoryDetected"`.
  - Complex @req or @story content → diagnostic only (preferImplements), no auto-fix.

4) Validation of @implements output:
- valid-annotation-format tests (tests/rules/valid-annotation-format.test.ts) confirm the shape produced by auto-fix is valid:
  ```ts
  name: "[REQ-IMPLEMENTS-PARSE] valid single @implements with one story and one requirement (default patterns)",
  code: `/**\n * @implements docs/stories/010.2-DEV-MULTI-STORY-SUPPORT.story.md REQ-IMPLEMENTS-PARSE\n */`,
  ```
- Auto-fix in prefer-implements-annotation produces `@implements  `, matching this validated format.

5) Documentation / migration guide: docs/rules/prefer-implements-annotation.md
- Linked to this story and requirements:
  ```md
  @story docs/stories/010.3-DEV-MIGRATE-TO-IMPLEMENTS.story.md
  @req REQ-OPTIONAL-WARNING
  @req REQ-MULTI-STORY-DETECT
  @req REQ-AUTO-FIX
  @req REQ-SINGLE-STORY-FIX
  @req REQ-PRESERVE-FORMAT
  @req REQ-VALID-OUTPUT
  @req REQ-BACKWARDS-COMPAT-VALIDATION
  ```
- Describes behavior, auto-fix examples, and configuration options that match the story’s intent (warn/cannotAutoFix/multiStoryDetected messages; examples of @story/@req → @implements transformation).
- Crucially, the config example claims:
  ```js
  // Default: off (no recommendations)
  "traceability/prefer-implements-annotation": "off",
  ```
  and text: "Default: off (no recommendations) – rule is disabled; no additional diagnostics".
- This directly conflicts with src/index.ts, where recommended/strict configs enable the rule at "warn" by default.

6) Story requirements that are not correctly met:
- Story acceptance: "Configurable Enforcement: Allow configuration of recommendation level (off, warn, error) - default off to maintain backward compatibility".
- Implementation notes: "Rule is **disabled by default** to maintain backward compatibility".
- Actual behavior: plugin’s shipped configs set `traceability/prefer-implements-annotation` to "warn" by default, not "off".
- Edge case described in story implementation notes: "@req without matching @story (warn, cannot auto-fix)" is not implemented; current code ignores such comments (`if (!hasStory || !hasReq) { return; }`).
